      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and your patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nCan you tell me which of these you meant?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day, a common target dose.\n- **500 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nIf you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
