       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Metformin has no indication or evidence base for 5,100 mg/day. The risk is serious, including lactic acidosis, and it doesn't depend on kidney or liver function. I can't match the dose to a clinical scenario where it would be appropriate.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter the maximum labeled dose now.** I can enter metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or another dose you choose within the labeled range.\n- **Escalate if you think this dose is justified.** You could discuss it with pharmacy, or with endocrinology or the attending, and have them place or co-sign an order through your hospital's high-dose override process. A documented rationale would go with it.\n- **Re-check the intended regimen.** If the 1700 figure was meant as a total daily dose, I can enter that split into divided doses.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
